,"journal":"Trials","paperid":"583","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170680762"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Other Hospitals","Private Research","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","mental health services","monsenso aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-56a2bca2-2334-4e88-affb-83050488a27b","ku-2a461911-082c-418b-b31f-c0c2886368ac"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effect of smartphone-based monitoring and treatment including clinical feedback versus smartphone-based monitoring without clinical feedback in bipolar disorder : the SmartBipolar trial—a study protocol for a randomized controlled parallel-group trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.29-698118","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The heterogeneity of the SARS-CoV-2 immune responses has become considerably more complex over time and diverse immune imprinting is observed in vaccinated individuals. Despite vaccination, following the emergence of the Omicron variant, some individuals appear more susceptible to primary infections and reinfections than others, underscoring the need to elucidate how immune responses are influenced by previous infections and vaccination. IgG, IgA, neutralizing antibodies and T-cell immune responses in 1,325 individuals (955 of which were infection-naive) were investigated before and after three doses of the BNT162b2 vaccine, examining their relation to breakthrough infections and immune imprinting in the context of Omicron. Our study shows that both humoral and cellular responses following vaccination were generally higher after SARS-CoV-2 infection compared to infection-naive. Notably, viral exposure before vaccination was crucial to achieving a robust IgA response. Individuals with lower IgG, IgA, and neutralizing antibody responses postvaccination had a significantly higher risk of reinfection and future Omicron infections. This was not observed for T-cell responses. A primary infection before Omicron and subsequent reinfection with Omicron dampened the humoral and cellular responses compared to a primary Omicron infection, consistent with immune imprinting. These results underscore the significant impact of hybrid immunity for immune responses in general, particularly for IgA responses even after revaccination, and the importance of robust humoral responses in preventing future infections.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Pérez-Alós, Laura","Hansen, Cecilie Bo","Almagro Armenteros, Jose Juan","Madsen, Johannes Roth","Heftdal, Line Dam","Hasselbalch, Rasmus Bo","Pries-Heje, Mia Marie","Bayarri-Olmos, Rafael","Jarlhelt, Ida","Hamm, Sebastian Rask","Møller, Dina Leth","Sørensen, Erik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Hilsted, Linda Maria","Bundgaard, Henning","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Iversen, Kasper","Garred, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720457"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"previous immunity shapes immune responses to sars cov 000000000002 booster vaccination and omicron breakthrough infection risk","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-41342-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720457","identifier":[{"id":"37699890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10497567","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85170696898","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-615e7680-7b74-429a-b197-ae634c21f875"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83C16B1437CF0E27942745AA8841E9A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-41342-2","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/376456954/s41467_023_41342_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","Amer