a Leth","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Erik","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","locid":"ba497828-2322-4b15-bfae-1e8a8c3895e7","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","orcid":"0000-0001-5288-3851","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Ruth","key":"frikkeschmidtpau","last":"Frikke-Schmidt","locid":"bce2c3b4-6e08-46c7-96c6-7e385b0ec8b3","name":"Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Linda Maria","key":"hilstedpau","last":"Hilsted","name":"Hilsted, Linda Maria","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Henning","key":"bundgaardpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"254c7f8d-79dd-4a5d-870f-3ed78cb56464","name":"Bundgaard, Henning","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Susanne Dam","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Kasper Karmark","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","name_org":"Iversen, Kasper Karmark","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Peter","key":"garredpau","last":"Garred","locid":"854d72a7-c955-43b5-b455-b7ea1f9bcb1e","name":"Garred, Peter","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37699890"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-023-41342-2","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"5624","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170696898"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-615e7680-7b74-429a-b197-ae634c21f875"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Previous immunity shapes immune responses to SARS-CoV-2 booster vaccination and Omicron breakthrough infection risk","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720457","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Patients with severe mental illness (SMI) i.e. schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder, and bipolar disorder are at increased risk of severe outcomes if infected with coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). Whether patients with SMI are at increased risk of COVID-19 is, however, sparsely investigated. This important issue must be addressed as the current pandemic could have the potential to increase the existing gap in lifetime mortality between this group of patients and the background population. The objective of this study was to determine whether a diagnosis of schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder, or bipolar disorder is associated with an increased risk of COVID-19. A cross-sectional study was performed between January 18th and February 25th, 2021. Of 7071 eligible patients with schizophrenia, schizoaffective disorder, or bipolar disorder, 1355 patients from seven psychiatric centres in the Capital Region of Denmark were screened for severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) antibodies. A total of 1258 unvaccinated patients were included in the analysis. The mean age was 40.5 years (SD 14.6), 54.3% were female. Fifty-nine of the 1258 participants had a positive SARS-CoV-2 antibody test, corresponding to a adjusted seroprevalence of 4.96% (95% CI 3.87-6.35). No significant difference in SARS-CoV-2-risk was found between female and male participants (RR = 1.32; 95% CI 0.79-2.20; p = .290). No significant differences in seroprevalences between schizophrenia and bipolar disease were found (RR = 1.12; 95% CI 0.67-1.87; p = .667). Seroprevalence among 6088 unvaccinated blood donors from the same region and period was 12.24% (95% CI 11.41-13.11). SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence among included patients with SMI was significantly lower than among blood donors (RR = 0.41; 95% CI 0.31-0.52; p < .001). Differences in seroprevalences remained significant when adjusting for gender and age, except for those aged 60 years or above. The study is registered at ClinicalTrails.gov (NCT04775407). https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT04775407?term=NCT04775407&draw=2&rank=1.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Sass, Marie Reeberg","Juul, Tobias Søgaard","Skov, Robert","Iversen, Kasper","Harritshøj, Lene Holm","Sørensen, Erik","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Andersen, Ove","Ekstrøm, Claus Thorn","Ullum, Henrik","Nielsen, Jimmi","Hageman, Ida","Fink-Jensen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-466613"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Antibodies Viral blood","COVID 19 blood","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","SARS CoV 2 metabolism","Seroepidemiologic Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Infection Disease Preparedness"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sars cov 000000000002 seroprevalence among patients with severe mental illness a cross sectional study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0264325","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-466613","identifier":[{"id":"35231037","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8887729","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85125591627","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7a34d252-6db0-41da-af4f-c2bea6bc75dd"],"keyword":["Adult","Antibodies, Viral/blood","COVID-19/blood","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Humans","Male","Mental Disorders/blood","Middle Aged","SARS-CoV-2/metabolism","Seroepidemiologic Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-93BD5B70C1A3FD40D0A67B4030A578C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0264325","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/314056586/SARS.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Infection Disease Preparedness"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Emergency Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Reeberg","key":"sasspau","last":"Sass","name":"Sass, Marie Reeberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias Søgaard","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","name":"