esponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"kristiansenkristianpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Kristian","rank":87,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32939067"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-020-2688-8","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"7825","journal":"Nature","pages":"390-396","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"585"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091129874"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Lundbeck Pharma","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-778b3b91-27ef-4e2c-aad7-ed0421e0e6e1","dtu-0ae314d8-3cae-4be5-aa11-60a43e069920","ku-086ea951-1ff7-4440-8203-9f99493d1404","kum-7676ac2a-4676-46b2-ab01-84851f2058be","sdu-e91a6ec4-90a1-4c53-b09a-911db76d343d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Population genomics of the Viking world","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S05-095.94-021408","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Context: The vitamin D receptor (VDR) and enzymes involved in activation (CYP2R1, CYP27B1) and inactivation (CYP24A1) of vitamin D are expressed in ovary, testes, and spermatozoa. Objective: Determine responsiveness to 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 [1,25(OH)2D3] in spermatozoa from normal and infertile men, and identify the site of exposure and how 1,25(OH)2D3 influences sperm function. Design: Spermatozoa expressing VDR, CYP2R1, CYP27B1, and CYP24A1 were analyzed in normal and infertile men. 25-Hydroxyvitamin D (25-OHD), 24,25-dihydroxyvitamin D [24,25(OH)2D3], and 1,25(OH)2D3 were measured in serum, seminal fluid, cervical secretions, and ovarian follicular fluid. 1,25(OH)2D3 was tested on human spermatozoa. Setting: Tertiary center for fertility. Participants: Protein expression in spermatozoa and semen quality were assessed in 230 infertile and 114 healthy men. Vitamin D metabolites were measured in fluids from 245 men and 13 women, while 74 oocytes and 17 semen donors were used for sperm-function tests. Main Outcome Measures: VDR and CYP24A1 expressions in spermatozoa, fluid concentrations of 25-OHD, 24,25(OH)2D3, and 1,25(OH)2D3, and 1,25(OH)2D3-induced effects on intracellular calcium concentration ([Ca2+]i) and sperm-oocyte binding in vitro. Results: VDR and CYP24A1 were expressed in a >2-fold higher fraction of spermatozoa from normal than infertile men (P < 0.01). Concentrations of 25-OHD, 24,25(OH)2D, and 1,25(OH)2D3 were undetectable in seminal fluid but high in ovarian follicular fluid. Follicular concentrations of 1,25(OH)2D3 induced a modest increase in [Ca2+]i and sperm-oocyte binding in vitro (P < 0.05). Conclusion: Presence of VDR and CYP24A1 mainly in spermatozoa of higher quality supports that 1,25(OH)2D3 available in the female reproductive tract may promote selection of the best gametes for fertilization.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Bøllehuus Hansen, Lasse","Rehfeld, Anders","de Neergaard, Rosanna","Nielsen, John Erik","Iversen, Lea Hedegaard","Boisen, Ida Marie","Mortensen, Li Juel","Lanske, Beate","Almstrup, Kristian","Carlsen, Elisabeth","Berg, Anders Hayden","Jørgensen, Niels","Andersen, Anders Nyboe","Juul, Anders","Blomberg Jensen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-490550"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"selection of high quality spermatozoa may be promoted by activated vitamin d in the woman","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-490550","identifier":[{"id":"27977320","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85015176312","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a27c54d4-0e21-432b-9f56-c85270de98ad"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C76181FF992DFFBD3A0AD2334941822D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, ICMM Section 8"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hos